      "writtenOn": "2019-10-01T16:59:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There are only 2 values.  The first one (\"base\") is intended to just be retrieved once at init time, b/c those are the \"static\" values that are mainboard-dependent and shouldn\u0027t change.  Then after that, whenever the proper host event is received, this host command is used to get the new information (\"dynamic\") that has potentially changed and possibly calculate new power limit values.",
